    {
      "heading": "Evidence is not proof",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "One counterexample is enough to show a conjecture is false.",
          "write": "1 counterexample → false"
        },
        {
          "say": "Many cases that work are only evidence.",
          "write": "many cases = evidence"
        },
        {
          "say": "n squared plus n plus 41 gives primes from 0 to 39. Forty in a row!",
          "write": "n² + n + 41"
        },
        {
          "say": "But n equals 40 gives 1681. That's 41 times 41.",
          "write": "1681 = 41 × 41 ✗"
        },
        {
          "say": "To be certain, you need a proof that covers every case.",
          "write": "proof = every case"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Searching with a while loop",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Is 150 in the pattern 7, 13, 19, 25? The rule is 6n plus 1.",
          "write": "7, 13, 19, 25, …"
        },
        {
          "say": "The loop adds 6 while t is less than 150.",
          "write": "While t < 150: t = t + 6"
        },
        {
          "say": "It jumps from 145 to 151, right over 150.",
          "write": "145 → 151",
          "diagram": "diagrams/y8/maths/testing-number-patterns-with-algorithms-jumps.svg",
          "alt": "Jumps of 6 from 139 to 145 to 151 skip 150"
        },
        {
          "say": "So 150 is not in the pattern.",
          "write": "150 not in pattern",
          "draw": {
            "type": "numberline",
            "from": 136,
            "to": 154,
            "start": 145,
            "jump": 6
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Check. 149 over 6 isn't a whole number, so there's no such position.",
          "write": "149 ÷ 6 not whole ✓"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Watch out for these",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Many examples don't prove a pattern. Remember the forty successes, then a failure.",
          "write": "evidence ≠ proof"
        },
        {
          "say": "Constant term is first term take difference. Check with position 1.",
          "write": "first − difference"
        },
        {
          "say": "About right isn't enough. The position must be a whole number.",
          "write": "position must be whole"
        },
        {
          "say": "When a search loop stops, n is the position, not the term.",
          "write": "label your columns"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Remember",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Arithmetic patterns can be built with a loop.",
          "write": "output, then add"
        },
        {
          "say": "Term equals difference times position, plus first take difference.",
          "write": "d × n + (first − d)"
        },
        {
          "say": "One counterexample proves a conjecture false.",
          "write": "1 counterexample"
        },
        {
          "say": "Lots of examples are evidence. Only a proof makes it certain.",
          "write": "proof covers every case"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
